<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>$title</title>
<meta name="description" content="A community catalog of agent skills for developing formal-methods and automated-reasoning software.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header>
  <h1>$title</h1>
  <p class="lede">A community-maintained selection of agent skills for designing, developing,
  and maintaining formal-methods and automated-reasoning tools: logic solvers, theorem provers,
  model checkers, synthesis tools, computer algebra systems, and optimization software.</p>
  <nav aria-label="Project">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="$catalog_md_url">Catalog (Markdown)</a></li>
      <li><a href="$readme_url">README</a></li>
      <li><a href="$contributing_url">Contributing</a></li>
      <li><a href="$issues_url">Issues</a></li>
      <li><a href="$repo_url">Repository</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>
<main id="main">
  <section class="actions" aria-label="Get involved">
    <a class="action" href="$question_url">Ask a question</a>
    <a class="action" href="$request_url">Request a skill</a>
    <a class="action" href="$contributing_url">Contribute a skill</a>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h2 id="about-title">About this catalog</h2>
    <p>Skills here address the distinctive engineering needs of reasoning software: semantic
    correctness, certificates and witnesses, specification frontends, testing, symbolic or
    numerical assumptions, performance analysis, and reproducibility. Some packages are
    maintained in this repository; others are maintained upstream and linked.</p>
    <p>Read a skill's instructions and license before using it, and review any scripts before
    running them: installing a skill is a trust decision. For general-purpose coding skills, see
    the <a href="#general-resources">general development resources</a> below.</p>
    <p class="count">$count. Open requests for missing skills are tracked
    <a href="$requests_url">on GitHub</a>; they are requests, not available packages.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="badges-title">
    <h2 id="badges-title">Evidence labels</h2>
    <dl class="legend">
      <dt>Listed</dt><dd>Links to the reason the skill was included.</dd>
      <dt>Reviewed</dt><dd>Links to a recorded maintainer review of a stated version or scope.</dd>
      <dt>Reported useful</dt><dd>Links to an explicit user or project report of where it helped.</dd>
      <dt>Evaluated</dt><dd>Links to an evaluation with a stated task, result and scope. Evaluated means evaluated, not successful.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>These labels describe linked evidence; they are not a ranking and do not certify
    correctness, security, or effectiveness in your setting. See the
    <a href="$badges_url">badge rules</a> and <a href="$policy_url">catalog policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

$sections

  <section id="general-resources" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
    <h2 id="resources-title">General development resources</h2>
    <p>General-purpose skills and references, maintained upstream. They are linked
    here rather than cataloged because they are not specific to FM/AR software;
    check each one's license before use.</p>
    <ul class="resources">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/skills">Anthropic's skills collection</a>:
      general-purpose skills and examples. It contains both open-source and
      source-available material; check each skill's license.</li>
      <li><a href="https://agentskills.io/specification">Agent Skills specification</a>:
      the package format used by this collection.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/skills/blob/main/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md">Anthropic's Skill Creator</a>:
      help with authoring and revising skills.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail">Ponytail</a>: makes an agent
      reuse existing code, the standard library, and platform features before writing
      new code. MIT licensed.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/blader/humanizer">Humanizer</a>: removes signs of
      AI-generated writing from text, useful for documentation and skill prose.
      MIT licensed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Other well-chosen collections can be proposed through a pull request that
    edits <code>site/index.html.in</code>.</p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer>
  <p>This catalog was started at
  <a href="https://www.dagstuhl.de/en/seminars/seminar-calendar/seminar-details/26431">Dagstuhl Seminar 26431,
  <cite>Automated Reasoning in Arithmetic: Logic, Algorithms, Software</cite></a> (18&ndash;23 October 2026).</p>
  <p>An independent FM/AR community initiative. Its organization is inspired by
  Anthropic's skills repository; it is not an official Anthropic project. Each skill is
  governed by its own stated license.</p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
